 but having an updated document would definitely benefit everyone who interacts with me. Let’s dive in!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Dbw0nDiVYFbDNR9GVflbLsaB|fc_08e3a97e327a8eb20169baba69551881919092aeb0efe7331f","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md","old_string":"3. Determine the Telegram chat target for any analyzer image reply.\n   - Prefer `--telegram-target` or `TELEGRAM_TARGET` when available.\n   - If no explicit target is provided, fall back to the Telegram user id so direct-chat execution still works without extra arguments.","new_string":"3. Determine the Telegram chat target for any analyzer image reply.\n   - Prefer an explicit `--telegram-target` taken from the current inbound request context.\n   - Do **not** rely on a process-wide `TELEGRAM_TARGET` default, because it can send images to a stale or fixed chat.\n   - If no explicit target is provided, fall back to the Telegram user id so direct-chat execution still works without extra arguments."},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md\",\"old_string\":\"3. Determine the Telegram chat target for any analyzer image reply.\\n   - Prefer `--telegram-target` or `TELEGRAM_TARGET` when available.\\n   - If no explicit target is provided, fall back to the Telegram user id so direct-chat execution still works without extra arguments.\",\"new_string\":\"3. Determine the Telegram chat target for any analyzer image reply.\\n   - Prefer an explicit `--telegram-target` taken from the current inbound request context.\\n   - Do **not** rely on a process-wide `TELEGRAM_TARGET` default, because it can send images to a stale or fixed chat.\\n   - If no explicit target is provided, fall back to the Telegram user id so direct-chat execution still works without extra arguments.\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":148,"output":204,"cacheRead":26624,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26976,"cost":{"input":0.00037000000000000005,"output":0.0030600000000000002,"cacheRead":0.006656,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.010086}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773845092856}}
{"type":"message","id":"12f8dbb5","parentId":"eab3fff0","timestamp":"2026-03-18T14:44:58.702Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Dbw0nDiVYFbDNR9GVflbLsaB|fc_08e3a97e327a8eb20169baba69551881919092aeb0efe7331f","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced text in ~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  23    - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\n  24    - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\n  25    - Also use that same numeric Telegram id as the default Telegram send target so the downloaded image goes back to the same DM conversation unless `--telegram-target` explicitly overrides it.\n  26 3. Determine the Telegram chat target for any analyzer image reply.\n- 27    - Prefer `--telegram-target` or `TELEGRAM_TARGET` when available.\n+ 27    - Prefer an explicit `--telegram-target` taken from the current inbound request context.\n+ 28    - Do **not** rely on a process-wide `TELEGRAM_TARGET` default, because it can send images to a stale or fixed chat.\n  28    - If no explicit target is provided, fall back to the Telegram user id so direct-chat execution still works without extra arguments.\n  29 4. Upload the image with a `POST multipart/form-data` request to:\n  30    - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\n  31 4. Read the upload response JSON and build the remote image path by concatenating:\n     ...","firstChangedLine":27},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773845098697}}
{"type":"message","id":"112d313b","parentId":"12f8dbb5","timestamp":"2026-03-18T14:45:02.056Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_08e3a97e327a8eb20169baba6bafd08191a7ac7426a0fdab1b\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpurpsEEIEuNza09cCTIsTNtlUSm5LR9Z9I4FhBi9FbkokCEq9QGH3Qd23aKvjmkMo-cA5a8aZl04ZC0b_j294TRStNMAqJKy4z6KHK53QIxjusKkJ3XnAocj4oIZHu1la5StovpKvjE_l-nhEMzOFV_591g7xQzXrVSAnQkWLVfvCaOeVaq_FS-1TSyyxvipirqLD0SphmYTKAwknUqju2lU4u9WHfikpoOPT59QEgO69CbCgg5dcydCT6necS2TRYvyeCjdlJf-mMEXjLotY6W6QRAjgiZI6CTa52ZY1Q4tW8f6XmJWp7_hGGohkz37QabKwHUnJHOGGOYYpIE1huoxoRiM_TckRszG-SaUnBHFLG2TzvoZdzl4li42OixBlTCyz6cZFyaikkxISqZT_rEfiU-2-W7_MfAFAl4PH0GQeRU6CTuWEsf_lv7Feu4penextAH87M9LQafxzKDqx0czKs01p9B8SmftqWBSqnTBFv1hYVSoHzUtIj-dov7Regm18MaI1mxgBRBG9d-xLtGpk7p-bTmNuWk_hfji7XnodvxS3EiE9o7Kwod4Z2qKBe_LWa9LtypVtPGjJCqJCqt-kV3TS2luunEisbRZ2CPJE3Zshx8cyj7yG0AWZa7WYc2u_BscpFre8bZVNHar-fKkw72DXkek7SYE_AxzvfwxG_ZJyIElfOZhSW8kS5rUQDnsKIEi-WG80JSTWE8O4b7gFbmU--tVgnzgKc8XSKqf4ipENXQbTL5P0kyGSy17U2woqJgIZmAfLkQbgKBDMejKVuTjc-f5cacg7EIMttPgvU2OOCJBkrbBrcaGFt-eoZrG7Ogut374F2AYHvc4Mcdi5Y1peCDld-Zpka__Co3iI81Wo3Iv5Tqc_RT0LSvDcJo5TP00FN6Y-FwX7dbUY4xPoKA==\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Good catch — I found the issue and fixed it.\n\nThe problem was that the pipeline script could pick up a global `TELEGRAM_TARGET` from the environment, which risks forwarding the analyzer image to an old/fixed chat instead of the current conversation. I removed that implicit target source, so future runs will use the current request’s chat target explicitly, with fallback only to the requesting Telegram user in direct chats.\n\nIf you want, I can now rerun the pipeline once with the corrected forwarding behavior.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_08e3a97e327a8eb20169baba6c390c8191ac2870c037d2a518\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":128,"output":127,"cacheRead":26880,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27135,"cost":{"input":0.00032,"output":0.001905,"cacheRead":0.006719999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.008945}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773845098700}}
